    <briefdescription>
<para>libor-forward-model process </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>stochastic process of a libor forward model using the rolling forward measure incl. predictor-corrector step</para><para>References:</para><para>Glasserman, Paul, 2004, Monte Carlo Methods in Financial Engineering, Springer, Section 3.7</para><para>Antoon Pelsser, 2000, Efficient Methods for Valuing Interest Rate Derivatives, Springer, 8</para><para>Hull, John, White, Alan, 1999, Forward Rate Volatilities, Swap Rate Volatilities and the Implementation of the Libor Market Model (<ulink url="http://www.rotman.utoronto.ca/~amackay/fin/libormktmodel2.pdf">http://www.rotman.utoronto.ca/~amackay/fin/libormktmodel2.pdf</ulink>)</para><para><xrefsect id="test_1_test000025"><xreftitle>Tests</xreftitle><xrefdescription><para>the correctness is tested by Monte-Carlo reproduction of caplet &amp; ratchet NPVs and comparison with Black pricing.</para></xrefdescription></xrefsect></para><para><xrefsect id="caveats_1_caveats000068"><xreftitle>Warning</xreftitle><xrefdescription><para>this class does not work correctly with Visual C++ 6.</para></xrefdescription></xrefsect></para>    </detaileddescription>
